{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And he shall wring its neck — the Sages explained how, from the fact that it is written: ומלק את ראשו, 'and he shall wring its head,' and not written ומלק אותו, 'and he shall wring it,' as it is written: ושחט אותו. Dunash explained: this is a proof for the words of our Sages, who observed the Temple service, that he cuts with his fingernail its spine and neck from behind, until he reaches the throat and descends and cuts until he reaches the signs and cuts them." "And he shall drain — of a soft thing it is fitting to say thus, as it is written: את קובעת כוס התערלה שתית מצית. But the dregs — one drains [them with effort]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:12.585473536Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}